  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clock) ((State == MEM) && (opcode == BEQZ)) |-> (Cond == (A == 16'd0)); endproperty",
      "explanation": "This establishes the branch comparison result one cycle before the target requires it. Every entry into MEM comes from EX, where BEQZ assigns Cond from A == 0 while A and IR remain unchanged. The lemma holds initially because State is IF, and its induction step follows directly from that EX update. For the target, the only transition that changes State[2] from zero to one is MEM to WB; this transition preserves A, IR, and Cond, so the lemma supplies the required equality. Transitions that keep State[2] high also preserve these registers, allowing the target to preserve itself. Thus this lemma conjoined with the target is 1-inductive."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

